<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tadeusz Kościuszko</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tadeusz Kościuszko was a Polish-Lithuanian military engineer and commander who also served in the American War of Independence. In 1794 he led a national insurrection against Russian and Prussian domination of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. The uprising's defeat was followed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-partition-of-poland">Third Partition</a> of 1795, which ended the Commonwealth's existence, and Kościuszko became an enduring symbol of Polish national resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tadeusz-kosciuszko.jpg" alt="Tadeusz Kościuszko" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Gottlieb Schweikart · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_G_Schweikart_-_Tadeusz_Ko%C5%9Bciuszko_(%C3%96aL).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
